-- title:
--   Induced-character table for the lift-trace seed over the cubic field
-- statement:
--   Let $L$ be a number field, Galois over $\mathbb{Q}$, equipped with a group isomorphism $e$ from $\mathrm{Gal}(L/\mathbb{Q})$ onto $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{Z}/3)$, and let `sylowH e` and `P2.c8H e` be the subgroups of $\mathrm{Gal}(L/\mathbb{Q})$ consisting of those $\gamma$ whose image $e\gamma$ is the reduction modulo the norm-$3$ prime of $\mathbb{Z}[\sqrt{-2}]$ of some matrix in the $16$-element set `P16`, resp. in the $8$-element set `C8`; write $K =$ `fixFld (sylowH e)` and $K' =$ `fixFld (P2.c8H e)` for their fixed fields inside $L$, assumed related by an algebra structure compatible with their inclusions into $L$. Let $\iota =$ `iotaZsqrtdNegTwo` $:\mathbb{Z}[\sqrt{-2}]\to\mathbb{C}$ be the ring map sending $\sqrt{-2}$ to $\sqrt{2}\,i$, and let $\zeta\in\mathbb{C}$ satisfy $\zeta^4=-1$ and $\zeta+\zeta^3=\sqrt{2}\,i$. The Hecke eigensystem `P2.liftTraceSeed e (sylowH e)` over $K$ with coefficients in $\mathbb{Z}[\sqrt{-2}]$ has level $\top$ and assigns to a prime $v$ of $\mathcal{O}_K$ the trace $a_v$ and determinant $b_v$ of a chosen matrix in the monoid generated by `Slift` and `Tlift` reducing to $e(\sigma_v)$, where $\sigma_v =$ `seedFrob (sylowH e) v` is the appropriate power of an arithmetic Frobenius above $v$; and `P2.artinValue e hζ 𝔓` is the value at `seedFrob (P2.c8H e) 𝔓` of the character `chiGal e hζ` of `P2.c8H e` attached to $\zeta$, a unit of $\mathbb{C}$. The assertion is that there is a finite set $S$ of primes of $\mathcal{O}_K$ such that for every $v\notin S$: first, for any two distinct primes $\mathfrak{P}_1\neq\mathfrak{P}_2$ of $\mathcal{O}_{K'}$ lying under $v$ one has $\iota(a_v)=\mathrm{artinValue}(\mathfrak{P}_1)+\mathrm{artinValue}(\mathfrak{P}_2)$ and $\iota(b_v)=\mathrm{artinValue}(\mathfrak{P}_1)\cdot\mathrm{artinValue}(\mathfrak{P}_2)$; and second, for any prime $\mathfrak{P}$ of $\mathcal{O}_{K'}$ lying under $v$ with residue degree `inertiaDeg'` equal to $2$ one has $a_v=0$ and $\iota(b_v)=-\,\mathrm{artinValue}(\mathfrak{P})$.
--
--   This is the local dictionary underlying Tunnell's octahedral construction: it records that the two-dimensional lift of $e$ restricted to the semidihedral subgroup is induced from the order-eight character of its cyclic index-two subgroup, in the form of the split and inert entries of the trace–determinant table at almost all primes of the cubic field $K$. The finite exceptional set comes from [`LanglandsTunnell.exists_finset_forall_inertia_eq_bot`](thm.html#LanglandsTunnell.exists_finset_forall_inertia_eq_bot), and the result feeds [`LanglandsTunnell.exists_quadratic_rayClassChar_table_liftTraceSeed_sylowH_of_detDictionaryRow`](thm.html#LanglandsTunnell.exists_quadratic_rayClassChar_table_liftTraceSeed_sylowH_of_detDictionaryRow), which rewrites the table in terms of a ray class character of the quadratic extension $K'/K$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_LanglandsTunnell_liftTraceSeed_sylowH_table_eq_artinValue.lean

